1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,792
Narrator: Scenario 88. Changes, security, and disaster recovery.

2
00:00:07,392 --> 00:00:18,744
A: We detected unusual logins and an unexpected process on one production host at 09:10 UTC. I have opened a restricted security incident record.

3
00:00:19,344 --> 00:00:31,464
B: Please preserve the relevant evidence and avoid uncoordinated changes. Have you recorded the host identifier, alert source, and timestamps without sharing sensitive details broadly?

4
00:00:32,064 --> 00:00:43,296
A: Yes. Those details are in the approved incident channel. I haven't rebooted the host or removed files because that could affect the investigation.

5
00:00:43,896 --> 00:00:54,120
C: That host handles part of our order traffic. If isolation is needed, can we remove it from service while the remaining hosts support demand?

6
00:00:54,720 --> 00:01:05,640
A: Current capacity suggests that is feasible, but I'll verify active connections and pending work first. We also need to identify any unique local state.

7
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:15,984
B: Follow the evidence collection steps in our response runbook using the approved tooling. I will decide the containment sequence with the incident lead.

8
00:01:16,584 --> 00:01:28,080
C: The service team can monitor order completion during the change. Please tell us which customer symptoms to watch and whether any queued work needs reconciliation.

9
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:40,056
A: I'll track failed submissions, completion delays, and the affected host's pending jobs. We won't replay transactions until we know their original processing status.

10
00:01:40,656 --> 00:01:52,512
B: The initial assessment supports isolating this host under our response procedure. Preserve access through the approved investigation path, and record each containment action.

11
00:01:53,112 --> 00:02:04,128
C: I acknowledge the service impact and will coordinate traffic removal with Ops. We'll validate that customers can still complete orders after the isolation.

12
00:02:04,728 --> 00:02:17,256
A: I'll execute the coordinated steps and log the results. Our next restricted update is at 09:40 UTC, including capacity, business checks, and pending evidence tasks.

13
00:02:17,856 --> 00:02:30,480
B: Thank you. We'll communicate only confirmed facts and keep the scope under investigation. Suspicious activity alone does not establish the full extent of compromise.
